[Music]  we're all crazy about Disney Princesses  everyone has their favorites and we love  seeing them reimagined as bad girls  real-life teenagers and even animals but  what if our favorite t-ara ladies were  transformed into handsome Prince's don't  forget to hit that subscribe button and  give this video a big thumbs up now  let's talk about Disney Princesses as  Disney princes so this is what a party  looks like Elsa frozen hit the big  screen and instantly became a classic  the whole world has caught the frozen  bug and we can't let it go  fans love the movie so much that they  spend hours creating art inspired by the  characters there are tons of images of  Elsa reimagined as a Snow King artist  Julia J m15 from tumblr created this fun  version of the beloved princess can you  get over those perfect blue eyes  that gorgeous plot them hair what really  grabbed our eye are the gorgeous suits  inspire by Elsa's gowns the Wardrobe in  these drawings perfectly captures the  style of the characters while playing up  their new gender it's not easy to turn a  sparkling ballgown into a perfectly  tailored suit but this artist totally  nails it Pocahontas Pocahontas is a  strong and brave princess she's a fierce  person imagine that incredible  personality in a hardened warriors body  Canadian artist Akemi Chan did and the  results are breathtaking we've loved  that tsukimi kept the characters long  hair the shaped sides of that undercut  would look just as great on the female  version of the character too the artist  also kept the beautiful shell necklace  we loved seeing a strong male character  with gorgeous accessories and a fierce  look Prince Pocahontas is spot-on he  still loves animals and is drawn with  his best friend split and Miko just like  his female counterpart he's strong  courageous and compassionate Jasmine  gender swapping Disney Princesses is a  hugely popular theme there does seem to  be a lot of similarities between styles  many princesses reimagined as princes  are drawn as delicate add raja'na smen  with clean shaven faces that's what  makes this version of jasmine so amazing  here we see the elegant princess as a  rugged enhanced  man who love the beard princesses redrew  as men rarely sport facial hair either  this unique take on the character is one  of the best ginger swaps we've ever seen  even Raja gets a fierce makeover male  Jasmine's characteristic fashion  translates well to we love the teal  jumpsuit deep cut v-neck and gold boots  men like to be gorgeous - after all  Tinkerbell artist Marian who is also  known online as galaxy speaking on  tumblr has gender swap - most of the  characters from Peter Pan her spunky  girl character Pat chirpin is just as  mischievous as the original character  she's reimagined Captain Hook's the  darling children and Smee but our  favorite is Tinkerbell her version of  the fairy is edgy tattooed and tough  we're loving the slightly rough looking  wings and moody expressions this version  of the character captures Tinker Bell's  tough attitude perfectly all of the  ethereal beauty is still there but in a  really masculine package Tinker Bell  makes a really fierce looking guy we  love how well the artist captures the  characters attitude in one facial  expression Merida  Merida is one of the most formidable  Disney characters ever written she's  courageous a skilled Archer and  obviously brave the character is  larger-than-life and unafraid to face  any challenge artists may be Chan  reimagines Merida as a tall rugged  Prince the character looks just as  capable of facing a bear we can't help  but wonder if Merida would have been  encouraged in her archery if she had  been a boy would she have been even more  skilled or is her talent so natural that  encouragement wouldn't make much a  difference either way this kilted  version looks just as fierce as his  female counterpart snow white snow white  is the original Disney Princess she  launched the brand and set the 